I have not seen the stable where Jerusalem the city of our Lord they say his life began; I've never seen;

Nor Nazareth the city where Nor Bethany where 'oft he found

He grew from child to man; retreat with friends serene;

Yet surer than the eye can see, Yet in my soul is bedded deep

My heart knows certainly that he This truth (that I shall ever keep)-

Was there—and lived for me. He is the shepherd of God's sheep.

I've never seen the winding Jordan I have not seen the garden where flow from Hermon's slope; He prayed in final hours;

Nor Galilee the beautiful where Nor Calvary where he was nailed 'oft he taught and spoke; and pierced by evil powers;

Yet in my heart there is no doubt, And yet unhesitatingly that in those lands he moved about I feel and know he set me free;

With men; but as the Son of God. Yes, even more, he died for me.
